<article class="prose-view">
    <h1>About Wayhop</h1>
    <p>Wayhop helps you get around Athens by public transport: live bus arrivals at the stops near you or any stop you look up, metro trips that show which carriage to ride for the exit, service announcements, and practical information like closing times, tickets and night buses.</p>

    <h2>Free, and ready for the underground</h2>
    <p>Wayhop is free and needs no account. Once you've opened them, the subway planner and the info page also work without a connection.</p>

    <h2>Where the information comes from</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Live bus arrivals, bus lines and stops:</strong> OASA's real-time service; the lines and stops are refreshed every night.</li>
        <li><strong>Metro and tram timetables:</strong> OASA's {{#external href="https://catalog.growthfund.gr/"}}open data{{/external}} ({{#external href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/deed.en" lang="en"}}CC BY 4.0{{/external}}), checked every night and converted for Wayhop. The first and last trains come from {{#external href="https://www.stasy.gr/"}}STASY{{/external}}'s timetables.</li>
        <li><strong>Service announcements:</strong> the {{#external href="https://www.oasa.gr/"}}OASA{{/external}} and {{#external href="https://www.stasy.gr/"}}STASY{{/external}} websites.</li>
        <li><strong>Elevators out of service:</strong> {{#external href="https://www.stasy.gr/elevators/"}}STASY's elevator page{{/external}}, read at most every 10 minutes, when someone needs it.</li>
        <li><strong>Which carriage to ride:</strong> collected for Wayhop. Where it isn't confirmed yet, the page says so.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Wayhop is an independent project, not affiliated with or endorsed by OASA, STASY or OSY. Times and arrivals can be wrong or out of date, so when it matters, check the announcements at the station too.</p>

    <h2>Accessibility</h2>
    <p>Wayhop aims to meet <abbr title="Web Content Accessibility Guidelines">WCAG</abbr> 2.2 level AA: every page works with a keyboard and a screen reader, in English and in Greek. If something doesn't work for you, please <a href="/contact">let us know</a>.</p>

    <h2>Open source</h2>
    <p>Wayhop's code is {{#external href="https://github.com/adiamandouros/move"}}public on GitHub{{/external}} under the GNU Affero General Public License v3 or later, and the data collected for it under CC BY-SA 4.0. It's built with Bootstrap (MIT License) and Google's Material Symbols (Apache License 2.0); the {{#external href="https://github.com/adiamandouros/move/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md"}}third-party notices{{/external}} list everything Wayhop uses.</p>

    <p class="small text-body-secondary mt-4">Created by {{#external href="https://github.com/adiamandouros"}}adiamandouros{{/external}}</p>
